.Dd October 4, 2026
.Dt MAGSAFE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm magsafe
.Nd control the light on an Apple MagSafe 3 cable
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -json
.Op Fl n
.Ar command
.Op Ar args ...
.Nm
.Fl h | -version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
controls the light on Apple's USB-C to MagSafe 3 cable (A2363) and reads the
cable's firmware state.
Color comes from the Mac's SMC; brightness and diagnostics come from fixed
messages to the cable.
It changes only the cable's RAM brightness and the Mac's light color setting,
never firmware or stored calibration.
.Pp
Commands that touch hardware run
.Nm
again through
.Xr sudo 8 ,
which may ask for a password.
Only one such command can run at a time.
Options can appear before or after the command.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm status
Show the firmware version, security flags, and light state.
.It Cm reset
Set both brightness scales to 100% and return color control to macOS.
Every step is attempted even if another fails.
.It Cm led set Ar mode
Set the light to
.Cm auto ,
.Cm off ,
.Cm green ,
or
.Cm amber .
.Cm auto
does not change brightness.
.It Cm led brightness Ar color percent
Light
.Cm green
or
.Cm amber
at 0 to 100% brightness, then wait up to 2 seconds for the cable's PWM output
to match.
.It Cm led blink Ar color
Switch between 100% and 0%, once per interval.
.Ar color
is
.Cm green ,
.Cm amber ,
or
.Cm alternate .
.It Cm led fade-in Ar color
Ramp up, switch off, then stay dark for the interval.
.It Cm led fade-out Ar color
Switch on, ramp down, then stay dark for the interval.
.It Cm led fade Ar color
Ramp up, ramp down, then stay dark for the interval.
.It Cm led get
Show the light mode, the two PWM outputs, and the color selector.
.It Cm firmware version
Show the cable firmware version.
.It Cm firmware security
Show the configuration-setter lock and signature-skip flags.
.It Cm firmware calibration
Show the four stored light calibration values.
.It Cm capabilities
List supported and unavailable functions.
.It Cm version
Show the
.Nm
version.
.It Cm help
Show a usage summary.
.El
.Pp
Blink and fade effects repeat until interrupted unless
.Fl -count
is given.
They select their color while dark, wait 450 ms for the cable's own color
transition, and end with
.Cm reset
on completion, error, or
.Dv SIGINT ,
.Dv SIGTERM ,
or
.Dv SIGHUP .
Fades check the PWM output at the top and bottom of every cycle.
.Pp
Diagnostics, brightness, and effects require cable firmware 3.2.0.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -json
Print the result, or the error, as one JSON object on standard output.
Commands that change the light print nothing on success without this option.
.It Fl n , Fl -dry-run
Check the command and print its plan without touching hardware or asking for a
password.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Show a usage summary.
.It Fl -version
Show the version.
.It Fl c , Fl -count Ar n
Number of blink or fade cycles: 1 to 300, or
.Cm infinite
(the default).
A finite effect must be planned to take 60 seconds or less.
.It Fl i , Fl -interval-ms Ar ms
Blink on and off time, or dark time after each fade cycle: 100 to 10000
(default 500).
.It Fl d , Fl -duration-ms Ar ms
Time for each fade ramp: 500 to 60000 (default 1000).
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /var/run/magsafe-cli.lock
Lock held while a hardware command runs.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 0
Success.
.It 1
Device, permission, or lock error.
.It 2
Invalid command, option, or value.
.It 128 + Ar n
An effect stopped by signal
.Ar n ,
such as 130 for Ctrl-C.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Set a dim green light:
.Dl $ magsafe led brightness green 25
.Pp
Alternate green and amber six times, 250 ms each way:
.Dl $ magsafe led blink alternate -c 6 -i 250
.Pp
Fade amber up and down until Ctrl-C:
.Dl $ magsafe led fade amber
.Pp
Show the plan of an effect as JSON, without touching hardware:
.Dl $ magsafe --json --dry-run led fade-in green -c 3 -d 2000
.Pp
Return the light to macOS:
.Dl $ magsafe reset
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr sudo 8
.Pp
.Lk https://github.com/mpopv/magsafe-cli
.Sh CAVEATS
.Nm
uses private Apple interfaces and has been tested on one Mac with one cable
firmware version.
